    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0458" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2614</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-05T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                                1918, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2008. Your 4196, August 31, 1 p.m. Mail to the Department texts and translations
                    of the secret archives and comment published in Dutch press.</p>
                <pb facs="0459" n="369" xml:id="pg369"/>
                <p>For your information and for such discreet use as you may deem advisable. There
                    is absolutely no foundation whatever for the statement that there is an
                    understanding between the United States and Japan regarding the Dutch East
                    Indies as compensation for Japan’s aid in Russia nor is there such an
                    understanding between any other governments so far as the American Government
                    knows.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
